// "DealtDamage" = generic (non-combat-narrowed) damage dealt to a recipient
// ([CR#120.1]) — the passive-voice recipient-subject phrasing ("<subject>
// is dealt damage"), as opposed to event/DealsCombatDamage's active-voice
// source-subject "<subject> deals combat damage to <recipient>". `source`
// and `combat` are left at their defaults (any source, combat unnarrowed),
// so this event fires on BOTH combat and noncombat damage to the recipient
// — matching the plain "is dealt damage" oracle phrasing (no card in this
// corpus narrows this event's source or amount). The recipient draws from
// the same player-identity/object grammar as DealsCombatDamage's recipient
// ([`filter::recipient_phrase`] on the migration-parser side).
// Usage: DealtDamage(to) — e.g. DealtDamage(Ref(This)), DealtDamage(Type("Creature")).
(
    name: "DealtDamage",
    template: "${0} is dealt damage",
    kinds: [EventFilter],
    params: [Predicate],
    body: Damage(to: Param(0)),
)
